== Problem description ==
<!-- 
Provide a concise description of the issue here. Be  as specific as possible to help readers quickly determine whether or not this is the exact problem they are facing.
 -->

iPhone 14 pro/ pro max boots normally but touchscreen does not respond at all. Display shows image, but there is no touch input on the entire panel. Replacing the screen does not fix the issue.

== Symptoms ==
<!--
Detail all measurable or observable symptoms in this section. 
-->
* Touchscreen not responding at all
* Screen replacement does not fix the problem
* GR on display connector is normal

== Solution ==
<!-- 
If the issue has a single, specific solution, provide it in this section and delete the sub-headers below. Otherwise, if there are multiple potential causes for the problem, outline the process of identifying the root cause and offer corresponding solutions below.

-->

The problem generally is due to a faulty capacitor that is placed on the touch boost line. Replacing the capacitor C9201 fixes the issue.
[[File:Bad cap iphone 14 pro max.png|center|thumb|306x306px|Bad Cap]]
[[File:The actual capacitor iphone 14 pro max.png|center|thumb|335x335px|The bad capacitor]]

=== Diagnostic Steps ===

# Check diode values on the connector, if you see any unusual reading trace it or else continue to the next step if all diode values are good.[[File:Diode value iphone 14 pro max.png|center|thumb|366x366px|Diode value]]
# Check for voltage on the PP_5V1_TOUCH_VDDTX_S2:
#* You cannot normally check voltage on this line
#* In order to check voltage on this line you have to manually enable the ic by giving it an enable signal and here is how to do it:[[File:Schematic Iphone 14 pro max touch boost.png|center|thumb|446x446px|Schematic ]]
#** Plug the DCPS cable/ battery to the phone 3.8-4.2 volts
#** Inject 1.8v at lowest possible Ampere on pin #31(according to JC DRAWING) to enable the LDO output[[File:Inject voltage iphone 14 pro max.png|center|thumb|Inject Voltage]]
#** Check the output voltage on pin #44(according to JC DRAWING)[[File:Output iphone 14 pro max.png|center|thumb|Touch Boost Output]]
#** If you get no voltage output then proceed to the repair steps<br />
=== Repair Steps ===

# Split the board in half
# Check the capacitor C9201, if shorted it '''MUST''' be replaced.
'''<u>NOTE:</u>''' (if you don't replace this capacitor phone will still have no touch problem)[[File:Bad cap iphone 14 pro max.png|center|thumb|Bad Cap]]
# Recheck for shorts
# In some rare cases of which short is not cleared:
#* You have to replace the u9200
#* Check diode value under the ic before replacing it[[File:Values under touch ic iphone 14 pro max.png|center|thumb|Touch ic Diode]]
#* Replace the ic and the capacitor
# Test the touch function, it should be restored.